-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. SSL4GIE
   "A Study on Self-Supervised Pretraining for Vision Problems in Gastrointestinal Endoscopy",
   Edward Sanderson and Bogdan J. Matuszewski, IEEE Access, 2024 (doi:10.1109/ACCESS.2024.3381517).
   https://github.com/ESandML/SSL4GIE
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0.
   This repository started as a fork of SSL4GIE (commits by Edward Sanderson / ESandML, 2024). The
   classification fine-tuning code, the model wrappers (src/ssl4polyp/models/models.py,
   src/ssl4polyp/models/DPT_decoder.py) and the original LICENSE derive from it.

2. Masked Autoencoders (MAE)
   "Masked Autoencoders Are Scalable Vision Learners", Kaiming He et al., CVPR 2022.
   https://github.com/facebookresearch/mae
   Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
   License: Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0).
   Located in src/ssl4polyp/models/mae/ (pretraining, fine-tuning and utility code, with the
   modifications recorded in this repository's history). The MAE code itself credits DeiT
   (https://github.com/facebookresearch/deit) and BEiT (https://github.com/microsoft/unilm/tree/master/beit).

3. PyTorch Image Models (timm)
   Ross Wightman, https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
   License: Apache License, Version 2.0.
   Used as a dependency (timm 0.3.2 for MAE pretraining, timm 0.4.12 for fine-tuning): the ViT
   building blocks, the .npz weight loader for the SUP-imnet initialisation and the optimiser
   parameter groups come from timm. src/ssl4polyp/_compat.py and src/ssl4polyp/models/models.py contain
   compatibility code written against timm's interfaces.

4. DPT (Dense Prediction Transformers)
   "Vision Transformers for Dense Prediction", René Ranftl, Alexey Bochkovskiy and Vladlen Koltun,
   ICCV 2021. https://github.com/isl-org/DPT
   License: MIT.
   The readout and reassembly blocks in src/ssl4polyp/models/DPT_decoder.py (inherited from SSL4GIE)
   follow the DPT implementation. The decoder is not used by the classification experiments.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data and pretrained weights (not distributed in this repository)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The datasets (SUN Colonoscopy Video Database, PolypGen, HyperKvasir, ImageNet-1k/ILSVRC-2012) and the
pretrained weights (AugReg ViT-B/16, MAE ImageNet-1k, MAE HyperKvasir) are subject to their own terms of
use and must be obtained from their providers. data_packs/ contains only split definitions
(identifiers, labels and annotations derived from those datasets) and their hashes; see README.md.
